WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.544
Hello!

2
00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:07.206
Who

3
00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:11.266
are you? I'm

4
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:14.228
a gecko. Geckos

5
00:00:14.229 --> 00:00:19.273
are colorful lizards. Where

6
00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:22.274
do you live? Geckos

7
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:26.136
live all over the world. We

8
00:00:26.137 --> 00:00:30.782
like rain forests and deserts. But

9
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:36.246
some geckos live in cold places. What

10
00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:38.951
do you eat? Geckos

11
00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:42.627
eat lots of insects. We

12
00:00:42.628 --> 00:00:47.882
also like fruit and flower nectar. Your

13
00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:51.211
tail is cool! Our

14
00:00:51.212 --> 00:00:54.990
tails help us climb. And

15
00:00:54.991 --> 00:01:00.071
they protect us from enemies. How

16
00:01:00.072 --> 00:01:03.465
do your tails protect you?

17
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:08.104
Sometimes enemies grab our tails.

18
00:01:08.105 --> 00:01:12.063
We break off our tails to escape.

19
00:01:12.064 --> 00:01:16.639
They grow back quickly.

20
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.650
Do geckos make sounds?

21
00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:23.489
Yes. Many lizards hiss.

22
00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:28.018
But geckos also click and chirp.

23
00:01:28.019 --> 00:01:32.794
We can even bark!

24
00:01:32.795 --> 00:01:36.594
You have cute little toes!

25
00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:39.770
We have pads on our toes.

26
00:01:39.771 --> 00:01:44.679
The pads are sticky.

27
00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:52.309
That helps us climb—and stick to things.

28
00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.404
I see a tasty cricket.

29
00:01:55.405 --> 00:01:58.636
See you later.

30
00:01:58.637 --> 00:02:08.883
Good-bye, Gecko!

